    <summary>IEEE 1045-1992 SLOC analysis, test detection, HTML/PDF reports, and CI/CD integration</summary>
    <description>
oxide-sloc is a Rust-based local code analysis workbench.

**Features:**
- IEEE 1045-1992 source line counting across 60 languages
- Unit test detection and coverage reporting
- Rich HTML and PDF reports
- Localhost web UI (no cloud required)
- CI/CD integration for Jenkins, GitHub Actions, GitLab, Bitbucket, Azure Pipelines
- Artifact publishing to Artifactory, Nexus, S3, MinIO, Azure Blob
- REST API with OpenAPI specification
- Fully offline/air-gap capable — no internet required after install

**Usage:**
```
oxide-sloc analyze ./my-repo --plain
oxide-sloc serve              # opens web UI at http://127.0.0.1:4317
oxide-sloc completions powershell | Out-File -Encoding utf8 $PROFILE.d/oxide-sloc.ps1
```
    </description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/oxide-sloc/oxide-sloc/releases/tag/v1.6.15</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
